<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  EXAMPLE ONLY - not installed. Installing it is the operator's call.

  Observe-only D1 swing shadow (Sleeve S1), execution_authority: none.
  It builds no execution client, reads no secret and places nothing.
  Network: about 25 GET requests a run to data-api.binance.vision (one 1d klines
  call per universe member and held symbol; more on the first run of a month,
  when the universe is re-frozen and rejected census candidates are probed).
  The runner's transport guard refuses every other host, never follows a
  redirect and ignores netrc and proxy environment; the log line reports the
  observed requests per host. It has no Hyperliquid client: the HL universe
  comes from the local census CSV.

  Python runs isolated (-I): PYTHONPATH and other PYTHON* variables, the user
  site-packages and the script directory are not on the import path. The
  runner imports only the standard library, numpy, pandas and requests.

  Schedule: launchd StartCalendarInterval uses the host's LOCAL time zone. This
  host is America/New_York, so 20:10 local is 00:10 UTC under EDT and 01:10 UTC
  under EST; both are after the runner's 00:05 UTC settle point. The 22:10 run
  retries a day the first run deferred (a response without a later bar) or
  failed transiently, and records today's open if it was not yet available;
  after a complete first run it appends nothing (re-runs are idempotent).
  Change Hour for another zone. A missed run (host asleep or off) is caught up by the
  next run: the runner processes every completed UTC day since its last
  daily_mark.

  Census: copy census_perps.csv to the path below (keep its mtime, cp -p) and
  refresh it before each month's first run. The runner never calls Hyperliquid
  to refresh it; at a monthly freeze it stops (exit code 2) when the census was
  captured more than 7 days before the month started, and each universe_frozen
  event records the census sha256, mtime and age.

  Seeding (optional, recommended): before installing, run the same program
  arguments once by hand with the backfill-from option (for example from
  2026-01-01) into the empty ledger, so the book starts with the positions
  the rule holds today instead of a flat cold start. See the runner's help.

  Installing (operator only): copy this file without the .example suffix to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents and bootstrap it into the gui domain with launchctl.
  (XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen, so no flags are spelled here.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>local.hypervector.research.d1_shadow</string>
	<key>LowPriorityIO</key>
	<true/>
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Background</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/.venv/bin/python</string>
		<string>-I</string>
		<string>-u</string>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/scripts/d1_shadow_runner.py</string>
		<string>--ledger</string>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/research/d1_shadow/ledger.jsonl</string>
		<string>--census</string>
		<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/research/d1_shadow/census_perps.csv</string>
		<string>--book-equity</string>
		<string>4800</string>
		<string>--funding-apr</string>
		<string>0.1095</string>
	</array>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<false/>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/runtime/research/d1_shadow.log</string>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector/data/runtime/research/d1_shadow.log</string>
	<key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>Hour</key>
			<integer>20</integer>
			<key>Minute</key>
			<integer>10</integer>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Hour</key>
			<integer>22</integer>
			<key>Minute</key>
			<integer>10</integer>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>WorkingDirectory</key>
	<string>/Users/gestas/Prototypes/hypervector</string>
</dict>
</plist>
